# kbuild writes its products beside the source when the module is built here
# with a plain `make`, which the Makefile supports against the running
# kernel's build tree. None of it belongs to the history, and the extension
# ban in the commit hook does not cover the names without one.
*.ko
*.mod
*.mod.c
*.o
*.rlib
*.rmeta
.*.cmd
.tmp_versions/
Module.symvers
modules.order
